---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<Docs title="Overview">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-10">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Craig</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A local TUI for repo-backed agent work.</p>

    <p>
      Craig is a full-screen TUI that lets you run AI coding agents — Claude Code, Codex, Cursor — across
      one or many repos simultaneously. The TUI is the primary product: create tasks, attach to live agent
      sessions, inspect diffs, and monitor read-only review state without leaving the terminal. The command
      surface exists for automation, scripting, and agents that need to manipulate Craig's local environment directly.
    </p>

    <h2>Core features</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 mb-8">
    {[
      { title: "Parallel agents", body: "Multiple agents running at the same time, each in an isolated worktree. No conflicts, no waiting." },
      { title: "Polyrepo support", body: "Register all your repos. Drive agents across any of them from one TUI workspace." },
      { title: "Any agent runner", body: "Works with Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor. Switch runners per task." },
      { title: "Read-only review panel", body: "Files, Changes, and Review inspector panels. Inspect diffs, PR state, checks, and comments while the agent performs repo actions in its PTY." },
      { title: "Worktree isolation", body: "Every task is a real git worktree on its own branch. Reversible, trackable, mergeable." },
      { title: "Agent-facing commands", body: "The CLI mirrors core operations so Craig, scripts, or an agent can provision tasks and inspect state programmatically." },
    ].map(({ title, body }) => (
      <div class="border border-[#292e42] rounded-lg p-4 hover:border-[#3b4261] transition-colors">
        <p class="text-[#c0caf5] font-semibold text-sm mb-1">{title}</p>
        <p class="text-[#565f89] text-sm leading-relaxed">{body}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Get started</h2>
    <p>
      Head to <a href="/docs/install">Install</a> to get Craig running, then follow the
      <a href="/docs/quickstart">Quickstart</a> to run your first agent task.
    </p>
  </div>
  </div>
</Docs>
